{"id": "EUVD-2026-97655", "enisaUuid": "d73977b2-43b6-32ba-b88e-730c38170324", "description": "LibreNMS before 26.9.0 contains an SQL injection vulnerability that allows unprivileged users to inject SQL by supplying an array-valued notification_id parameter to notifications.inc.php. Attackers can perform cross-table reads of users.password hashes, with results persisted in notifications_attribs and readable through the interface.", "datePublished": "2026-10-12T16:05:35", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-13T16:19:23", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:H/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/librenms/librenms/security/advisories/GHSA-2pw7-8mmj-gcw5", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/librenms-before-26.9.0-sql-injection-via-notification-id-in-notifications-inc-php"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-109353", "GHSA-g9jw-2r94-hwjc"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.25, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1b555ab6-395a-3d27-8ced-c63e0329ffd9", "product": {"name": "librenms", "vendor": {"name": "librenms"}}, "product_version": "0 <26.9.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "da3e9b19-1aac-3b4a-a542-d6e7c10dac9f", "vendor": {"name": "librenms"}}], "isExploited": false}